| ---- Rule Metadata ----
| Rule Name: Lateral Movement via PsExec
| MITRE ATT&CK: T1021.002 (Lateral Movement — SMB/Windows Admin Shares)
| Severity: High
| Description: Detects PsExec service installation on remote hosts correlated with new network logon sessions
| Author: Vignesh R
| Created: YYYY-MM-DD
| ---- Search Logic ----

index=wineventlog sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" OR sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
    (EventCode=7045 OR EventCode=1 OR EventCode=3)
| eval detection_type=case(
    EventCode=7045 AND ServiceName="PSEXESVC", "psexec_service_install",
    EventCode=1 AND (Image="*\\psexec.exe" OR Image="*\\PsExec64.exe" OR ParentImage="*\\PSEXESVC.exe"), "psexec_process",
    EventCode=3 AND DestinationPort=445 AND Image="*\\psexec.exe", "smb_connection",
    1=1, "other"
)
| where detection_type != "other"
| stats
    values(detection_type) AS detection_chain
    values(Image) AS processes
    values(DestinationIp) AS target_hosts
    values(User) AS executing_users
    earliest(_time) AS first_seen
    latest(_time) AS last_seen
    count AS event_count
    BY ComputerName
| where mvcount(detection_chain) >= 2
| eval severity="HIGH"
| table ComputerName, executing_users, target_hosts, detection_chain, processes, event_count, first_seen, last_seen

| ---- Alert Configuration ----
| Schedule: Every 5 minutes
| Alert condition: Number of results > 0
| Alert action: Create TheHive case (severity: HIGH), email SOC lead
| Throttle: 30 minutes per ComputerName

| ---- Tuning Notes ----
| - Whitelist IT admin workstations that legitimately use PsExec
| - Exclude known service accounts used for patch deployment
| - Consider adding PAExec and RemCom as PsExec alternatives
| - Correlate with Active Directory authentication logs for context
| - High false positive risk in environments using SCCM or similar remote admin tools
